{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 10, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " Title: A captivating journey through Japan\n\nLast fall, I had the opportunity to visit Japan, a country that had long been on my bucket list. The moment I stepped off the plane, I was struck by the unique blend of tradition and modernity that defines this fascinating nation.\n\nMy first stop was Tokyo, a bustling metropolis that is home to both ancient temples and towering skyscrapers. I visited the Meiji Shrine, a Shinto shrine nestled in a peaceful forest, where I took part in a traditional purification ceremony. The serenity of the shrine was a stark contrast to the energy of the city, which was on full display in the bustling streets of Shibuya and the neon-lit arcades of Akihabara.\n\n\nFrom Tokyo, I took a bullet train to Kyoto, the cultural heart of Japan. Here, I strolled through the picturesque streets of Gion, where geishas still walk the streets, and marveled at the intricate beauty of Kinkaku-ji, the Golden Pavilion. I also visited Fushimi Inari, a shrine dedicated to the Shinto god of rice, where I wandered through thousands of vermilion torii gates that snaked their way up the mountain.\n\n\nNo trip to Japan would be complete without trying the food, and I indulged in sushi, ramen, and okonomiyaki to my heart's content. I even took a cooking class, where I learned to make traditional Japanese dishes like tempura and miso soup.\n\nMy journey through Japan was a captivating blend of the old and the new, the traditional and the modern. I left the country with a newfound appreciation for its rich history and culture, as well as a desire to return and explore even more of this beautiful nation.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Title", "logprob": -0.007975990884006023}, {"token": ":", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.11001642793416977}, {"token": "capt", "logprob": -0.8246393203735352}, {"token": "iv", "logprob": 0.0}, {"toke